{
  "subject": {
    "slug": "orientation-to-radiation-therapy",
    "title": "Orientation to Radiation Therapy",
    "order": 3
  },
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "history-of-radiologic-technology",
    "title": "Rays of Discovery: History of Rad Tech",
    "order": 0,
    "pages": [
      {
        "title": "The Unseen World Revealed",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Purpose: Why This Matters This lesson explores the groundbreaking discoveries that launched the field of radiologic technology, allowing us to \"see\" inside the human body and harness new forms of energy for medicine."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Task: What You Will Do Journey through the late 19th and early 20th centuries to learn about X-rays, radioactivity, key scientists, and their initial medical applications."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Criteria for Success: How You'll Know You've Learned By the end, you should be able to identify discoverers of X-rays/radioactivity, describe their initial medical impact, and recognize the scope of radiologic sciences."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Radiologic technology encompasses diverse imaging and therapeutic applications, all built upon this foundational work."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "The Spark - Wilhelm Conrad Roentgen & X-rays (1895) \u2728",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "On "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "November 8, 1895",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ", German physics professor "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Wilhelm Conrad Roentgen",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " discovered X-rays while experimenting with cathode rays."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "attrs": {
                    "level": 4
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The Discovery:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Noticed a barium platinocyanide screen fluorescing near his covered Crookes tube."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Deduced unknown \"X-rays\" were penetrating cardboard and causing the glow."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Found rays passed through many objects but were blocked by denser materials (bone, metal). His first X-ray was of his wife's hand."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "attrs": {
                    "level": 4
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Impact:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "News spread rapidly. X-rays were quickly used to visualize bones, locate fractures, and detect foreign objects, marking the beginning of diagnostic radiology. Roentgen received the first Nobel Prize in Physics in 1901."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "q_page2_1_ans",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Quick Check: Who is credited with the discovery of X-rays in 1895?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "Marie Curie",
              "Henri Becquerel",
              "Wilhelm Conrad Roentgen"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explanation": null
          },
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Check Answer"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Unveiling Radioactivity - Becquerel & The Curies (1896+) \u269b\ufe0f",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Natural radioactivity was discovered shortly after X-rays."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "attrs": {
                    "level": 4
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Henri Becquerel (1896):"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Discovered that uranium salts emitted penetrating rays spontaneously, fogging photographic plates even in the dark. This was "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "natural radioactivity",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "attrs": {
                    "level": 4
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Marie and Pierre Curie:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Investigated Becquerel's rays, processing tons of pitchblende."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "In 1898, discovered "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "polonium",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " and "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "radium",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": ", elements far more radioactive than uranium."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Their work was foundational for understanding atomic structure. Marie Curie won Nobel Prizes in Physics (1903) and Chemistry (1911)."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "These discoveries paved new avenues for medical diagnosis and therapy."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Branching Out - Early Radiologic Modalities",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "X-rays and radioactivity spurred diverse medical applications."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "attrs": {
                    "level": 4
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Early Applications:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Radiography:",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " Immediate use for imaging bones and foreign bodies."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Fluoroscopy:",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " Real-time X-ray imaging to observe motion."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Early Radiation Therapy:",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " Experimental use of X-rays and radium to treat cancers and skin conditions."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Nuclear Medicine (Early Concepts):",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " Ideas of using internal radioactive sources for diagnosis/therapy emerged."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Advanced modalities like CT, MRI, and Ultrasound developed later, building on these crucial initial discoveries."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Early Professionals, Safety, & Standardization",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Rapid adoption brought needs for trained personnel and safety."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "attrs": {
                    "level": 4
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "First Professionals & Safety Awareness:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "\"X-ray technicians\" emerged as dedicated operators."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Early radiation users suffered burns and other effects, highlighting dangers (\"martyrs of radiology\") and spurring protection measures."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "attrs": {
                    "level": 4
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Standardization:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Radiological societies formed to share knowledge and address safety."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "The "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "American Registry of X-Ray Technicians",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " (ARRT precursor) was founded in "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "1922",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " to establish standards and credential technicians."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Summary & Next Steps \u27a1\ufe0f",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Key breakthroughs (1895-early 1900s):"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Roentgen's X-rays."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Becquerel's radioactivity."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "The Curies' work with radium and polonium."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "These led to diagnostic imaging, early RT, and the formation of professional bodies like the ARRT (1922)."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "attrs": {
                    "level": 4
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Transition to Radiation Therapy:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "How did these early therapeutic ideas evolve into modern Radiation Therapy? Explore this in our next lesson, \"Targeting Disease: The Evolution of Radiation Therapy.\""
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Test Your Knowledge: History Timeline Activity!"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
